Key Functional Changes
- Event Delegation and Standard Listeners: All button clicks and mouse movements are handled cleanly in the DOMContentLoaded script block. No inline onclick or onmousedown attributes exist in the markup.
- DOM Coordinate Rendering: Stamps are injected into the DOM as absolute-positioned div elements, replacing the static canvas drawing.
- Drag-and-Drop Interaction: Mousedown grabs the selected element, mousemove calculates the offset relative to the poster board to allow smooth, real-time repositioning, and mouseup locks it into place.
- Composition Feedback: A scoring function reads the exact style and coordinate properties of the active stamps. It rewards having a diverse set of stamps, keeping the item count between 3 and 7 to avoid visual clutter, and specifically looks for the Typography stamp being placed in the upper third of the canvas layout.
- Safe Export: Uses standard DOM methods to build the text and pushes the final layout brief to the clipboard via a safe, temporary textarea execution, avoiding innerHTML manipulation for user output.

